1
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:25,090
They’re going out with a bang.

2
00:08:38,181 --> 00:08:44,181
Ice Age: Collision Course is a adventure, animation,
family film directed by Mike Thurmeier.

3
00:12:57,272 --> 00:13:03,272
Set after the events of Continental Drift, Scrat's epic pursuit of his elusive acorn catapults him outside of
Earth, where he accidentally sets off a series of cosmic events that transform and threaten the planet.

4
00:17:16,363 --> 00:17:22,363
To save themselves from peril, Manny, Sid, Diego, and the rest of the herd leave their home and embark on a quest full of
thrills and spills, highs and lows, laughter and adventure while traveling to exotic new lands and locations.

5
00:21:35,454 --> 00:21:41,454
Manny (voice), played by Ray Romano.

6
00:25:54,545 --> 00:26:00,545
Sid (voice), played by John Leguizamo.

7
00:30:13,636 --> 00:30:19,636
Diego (voice), played by Denis Leary.

8
00:34:32,727 --> 00:34:38,727
Ellie (voice), played by Queen Latifah.

9
00:38:51,818 --> 00:38:57,818
Crash (voice), played by Seann William Scott.

10
00:43:10,909 --> 00:43:16,909
Eddie (voice), played by Josh Peck.

11
00:47:29,999 --> 00:47:35,999
Ice Age: Collision Course is a 2016 American animated
science-fiction comedy film produced by Blue Sky Studios.

12
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:55,090
The fifth in the Ice Age film series, it was directed by Michael Thurmeier,
and written by Michael Wilson, Michael Berg, and Yoni Brenner.

13
00:56:08,181 --> 00:56:14,181
Ray Romano, John Leguizamo, Denis Leary, Josh Peck, Simon Pegg, Seann William Scott,
Jennifer Lopez and Queen Latifah reprise their roles from the previous films.

14
01:00:27,272 --> 01:00:33,272
In the film, Scrat is propelled into outer space in an abandoned spaceship during an
attempt to bury his acorn and accidentally sends a giant asteroid towards Earth.

15
01:04:46,363 --> 01:04:52,363
Manny, the Herd and Buck must go on a life-or-death
mission to find a way to fend it off.

16
01:09:05,454 --> 01:09:11,454
The film premiered at the Sydney Film Festival on June 19, 2016, and was
theatrically released in the United States on July 22 by 20th Century Fox.

17
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
The film received generally negative reviews from critics and grossed
$408 million against a $105 million production budget.

18
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
While the film was deemed a disappointment at the American
box-office, it performed better internationally.

19
01:22:02,727 --> 01:22:08,727
A spin-off film, The Ice Age Adventures of Buck Wild, was released in 2022, while a
further sequel, Ice Age: Boiling Point, is scheduled to be released in 2027.

20
01:26:21,818 --> 01:26:27,818
The film explores themes of fire, fireworks, mammoth, sequel, prehistory.

21
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
